US-054 is still Partial, so I'm not emitting the completion signal.

The implementation is in place: the character controller, joints, and collision-cell work are in `engine/physics/src/`. The Linux gates passed on the last pass I could check against the current tree, which had no source change since then: `ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, and `linux-unit` (22 of 22). The Windows gates passed on an earlier pass.

Two acceptance criteria are open, and neither can be closed in this environment:

- **`linux-gcc` gate.** The Jolt code needs GCC 11 or newer. `/usr/bin` still has only GCC 9.4 and clang 10, so `linux-gcc`, `linux-gcc-debug`, and `linux-gcc-unit` cannot run here. This needs GCC 11+ installed or the CI job.
- **Performance measurement.** `engine_bench --suite acceptance` has no harness yet; that is US-074. The `physics_stress` scene is US-077.

I also did not run the `linux-asan` / `linux-sanitize` gate in this pass. The earlier notes record `linux-sanitize` failing in the X11 focus tests, which is unrelated to physics but still open.

I appended a short status entry to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`. No source files changed.
